erification.json"} {"question" "e-4406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, $C$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix and $D$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $C$ and $3$ rows in $D,$ so $C$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{3}}}{C} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\cdot} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{3}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{D} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{CD}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $CD,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-4=1\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,1=1\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 2 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-1=2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,4=2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13989257/example-4406.json" "file_sha256" "e517ee431410b5324334d829cd70212e1403483115776c909364ceeb3ab125d4" "basis" 992 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13989257/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $C=AB.$ What is the value of $c_{32}$, if\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13989257/example-4407.json" "file_sha256" "a65f3fc0cb670fd7cee239e88827fb65aa0089706c873a22883796632cffbee1" "basis" 992 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13989257/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying the $3$rd row in $A$ by the $2$nd column in $B$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot 4+2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =4-4 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13989257/example-4407.json" "file_sha256" "a65f3fc0cb670fd7cee239e88827fb65aa0089706c873a22883796632cffbee1" "basis" 992 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13989257/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the product \n $\\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n       -1 \\\n \t0 \\\n        -2\n \t\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        2 & -5\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13989257/example-5885.json" "file_sha256" "bdfff508f03b59f8de484ba5ef5c267c62cefa35bd00f493fbe01fb73ddcab6f" "basis" 992 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13989257/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, the first factor is a $3 \\times 1$ matrix and the second factor is a $1 \\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in the first matrix and $1$ row in the second matrix, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times {\\color{green}\\fbox{1}} {\\color{green}\\checkmark} {\\color{green}\\fbox{1}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} = \n\t\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign {\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n       -1 \\\n \t0 \\\n        -2\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        2 & -5\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n\t&= \n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        (-1)\\cdot 2 & (-1)\\cdot (-5) \\\n        0\\cdot 2 & 0\\cdot (-5)\\\n        (-2)\\cdot 2 & (-2)\\cdot (-5)\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack \\[5pt]\n\n\t&=\n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n       -2 & 5 \\\n       0 &  0 \\\n       -4 &  10 \n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack \n}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13989257/example-5885.json" "file_sha256" "bdfff508f03b59f8de484ba5ef5c267c62cefa35bd00f493fbe01fb73ddcab6f" "basis" 992 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13989257/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-317847" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine $AB$ given that \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-317847" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the unknown elements of $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,5=2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot 5 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,7=4\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-317847" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e6c172c2caa6d0d0725c2b891546114c170f4d73ee6417c0178db562015d18c"} {"question" "q-317847" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-317847" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "