nTherefore, \n$XY=[\\begin{aligned}22 & 9\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-129496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e6c172c2caa6d0d0725c2b891546114c170f4d73ee6417c0178db562015d18c"} {"question" "q-129496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-129496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 12\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}12 & 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}15 & 9\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}22 & 9\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-129496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}22 & 9\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-317848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine $AB$ given that \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $-6$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $11$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-317848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix and $B$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $A$ and $4$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the unknown elements of $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 11 & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-4=1\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 11 & -2\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-2=4\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 11 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-317848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e6c172c2caa6d0d0725c2b891546114c170f4d73ee6417c0178db562015d18c"} {"question" "q-317848" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-317848" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-317848" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-317848" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-1035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $ST$,  if  $S=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-1035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, $S$ is a $1\\times 4$ matrix and $T$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $S$ and $4$ rows in $T,$ so $S$ and $T$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{T}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={ST}_{1\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $ST,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}24 & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,24=2\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}24 & 1\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,1=2\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$ST=[\\begin{aligned}24 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-1035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e6c172c2caa6d0d0725c2b891546114c170f4d73ee6417c0178db562015d18c"} {"question" "q-1035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-1035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-20 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}12 & -24\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}20 & 24 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}24 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-1035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}24 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-70949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $K=MN.$ What is the value of ${k}_{12}$, if\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,N=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -5\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-70949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying the $1$st row in $M$ by the $2$nd column in $N$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}_{12} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-1)+(-4)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-5+8 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-70949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/dif