n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{13} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 10 & 2 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 3+3\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-6-6+5 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-130111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e6c172c2caa6d0d0725c2b891546114c170f4d73ee6417c0178db562015d18c"} {"question" "q-130111" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-130111" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-130111" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-318462" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $P=QR.$ What is the value of ${p}_{31}$, if\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\n${p}_{31}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-318462" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying the $3$rd row in $Q$ by the $1$st column in $R$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}_{31} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2(5)+1(-3)+(-2)(1) \\\\  & =10-3-2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-318462" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e6c172c2caa6d0d0725c2b891546114c170f4d73ee6417c0178db562015d18c"} {"question" "q-318462" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-318462" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-275547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $L=MN.$ What is the value of ${l}_{22}$, if\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,N=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\n${l}_{22}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-275547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying the $2$nd row in $M$ by the $2$nd column in $N$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{l}_{22} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =8+6 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-275547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e6c172c2caa6d0d0725c2b891546114c170f4d73ee6417c0178db562015d18c"} {"question" "q-275547" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-captu