ed}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-10\\cdot 1 & -10\\cdot (-5) & -10\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 6\\cdot 1 & 6\\cdot (-5) & 6\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 0\\cdot 1 & 0\\cdot (-5) & 0\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 8\\cdot 1 & 8\\cdot (-5) & 8\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 50 & 10 \\\\ 6 & -30 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -40 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-1038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e6c172c2caa6d0d0725c2b891546114c170f4d73ee6417c0178db562015d18c"} {"question" "q-1038" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-1038" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & -30 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & -50 & -10 \\\\ 6 & -30 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -40 & -8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 50 & 10 \\\\ 6 & -30 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -40 & -8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 50 & 10 \\\\ 6 & -30 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["text" "Undefined"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-1038" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 50 & 10 \\\\ 6 & -30 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -40 & -8\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-275548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $AB,$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-275548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, $A$ is $3\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix.  \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $A$ and $1$ row in matrix $B$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1\\cdot 1 & 1\\cdot (-2) \\\\ 2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot (-2) \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 1 & (-2)\\cdot (-2)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfbcf7b6e5c1f7aa53f14785f46e107e947eba6c126c52ca1290c2fd9cec4692"} {"question" "q-275548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "va