e/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/assets/b99016bca94adc5de11eddef950fa13fc4349aaf95387468d07f294c409d029d.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/example-4406.json" "file_sha256" "aecbae001ca1c2e661aab2da710381d6aec22b65953aa4135f58340866994943"} {"question" "e-4406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, $C$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix and $D$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $C$ and $3$ rows in $D,$ so $C$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{3}}}{C} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\cdot} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{3}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{D} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{CD}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $CD,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-4=1\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,1=1\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 2 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-1=2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,4=2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/assets/64b831a66cdd9a3176d1eb916dfae189b41eb1f0f3ed3184797f92e404957878.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/example-4406.json" "file_sha256" "aecbae001ca1c2e661aab2da710381d6aec22b65953aa4135f58340866994943"} {"question" "e-4407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $C=AB.$ What is the value of $c_{32}$, if\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/assets/c6c7e580cfd96bc23c55742535ceb40a94635c2a44b911e0d08311c3a599c2fa.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/example-4407.json" "file_sha256" "c0c51edf8974fd6de1489ec6ee3f2786c4fdb41456347570b049fd43315fbf39"} {"question" "e-4407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying the $3$rd row in $A$ by the $2$nd column in $B$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot 4+2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =4-4 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/example-4407.json" "file_sha256" "c0c51edf8974fd6de1489ec6ee3f2786c4fdb41456347570b049fd43315fbf39"} {"question" "e-5885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the product \n $\\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n       -1 \\\n \t0 \\\n        -2\n \t\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        2 & -5\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/example-5885.json" "file_sha256" "f49cfedf956b51f500dd473802a005c263698e9106dad5042788f872eccc1649"} {"question" "e-5885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, the first factor is a $3 \\times 1$ matrix and the second factor is a $1 \\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in the first matrix and $1$ row in the second matrix, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times {\\color{green}\\fbox{1}} {\\color{green}\\checkmark} {\\color{green}\\fbox{1}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} = \n\t\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign {\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n       -1 \\\n \t0 \\\n        -2\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        2 & -5\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n\t&= \n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        (-1)\\cdot 2 & (-1)\\cdot (-5) \\\n        0\\cdot 2 & 0\\cdot (-5)\\\n        (-2)\\cdot 2 & (-2)\\cdot (-5)\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack \\[5pt]\n\n\t&=\n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n       -2 & 5 \\\n       0 &  0 \\\n       -4 &  10 \n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack \n}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043519/example-5885.json" "file_sha256" "f49cfedf956b51f500dd473802a005c263698e9106dad5042788f872eccc1649"}] "usage" {"q-129495" [] "e-4407" [] "e-4406" [] "q-13635" [] "e-5885" []} "basis" 1618 "retractions" [[17592186100607 :question/problem "Find $CD$, if \n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]$"] [17592186100607 :question/worked-solution "Here, $C$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix and $D$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $C$ and $3$ rows in $D,$ so $C$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{3}}}{C} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\cdot} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{3}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{D} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{CD}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $CD,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-4=1\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,1=1\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 2 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-1=2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,4=2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]$"] [17592186100608 :question/problem "Let $C=AB.$ What is the value of $c_{32}$, if\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186283269 17592186283270 17592186283271 17592186283272 17592186283273 17592186283297 17592186283298 17592186283299 17592186283300 17592186283301] "immutable_fields" [[17592186283268 :answer-field/correct] [17592186283268 :answer-field/id] [17592186283268 :answer-field/key] [17592186283268 :answer-field/type] [17592186283296 :answer-field/correct] [17592186283296 :answer-field/id] [17592186283296 :answer-field/key] [17592186283296 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
